{
  "$description": "Spacing-binding census of the LIVE SAMAVESH Figma library (fileKey 3FF5l0SMNIwdpZrKkeyPTm). For every auto-layout frame on every page, the six spacing properties (paddingLeft/Right/Top/Bottom, itemSpacing, counterAxisSpacing) are classified as: tier2 (a correct semantic space token), tier1 (a hidden ref/space|ref/size primitive), crossFamily (a radius/type/colour variable bound to a spacing property), ghost (a local variable id no collection owns), remote (a variable imported from another library) or raw (unbound, non-zero). Zero-valued unbound properties are not counted — an auto-layout frame defaults every padding to 0 and counting those would drown the signal.",
  "$sweptAt": "2026-08-17",
  "$note": "SECOND census, taken after the ref/radius/none rebind of 2026-08-17. Every ref/radius/none binding on a spacing property, across 38 pages, was moved to padding/none · inline/none · stack/none, chosen by property and layout axis (padding* → padding/none; itemSpacing → inline on a HORIZONTAL frame, stack on a VERTICAL one; counterAxisSpacing → the opposite axis). Zero visual change: ref/radius/none and all three semantic none tokens resolve to 0, and the script refused to touch any property whose value was not already 0. Mains were rebound first; instance descendants carrying EXPLICIT overrides were then corrected directly, because an override does not follow its main — that accounted for ~13,500 of the total, Dropdown alone 7,098. MEASURED RESULT: crossFamily 38,799 → 5,968; tier2 4,568 → 37,632; correct semantic spacing 6.96% → 57.51%. Zero ref/radius/none bindings remain on any spacing property on any page. What is LEFT in crossFamily is the NON-zero radius rungs (ref/radius/md · xs · sm · xxs) bound to spacing — chiefly Dropdown 2,924, Pagination 503, Stepper 468, List 438. Those carry real values and cannot be moved without choosing a space rung of equal value, so they are a separate job.",
  "$method": "ONE PAGE PER use_figma INVOCATION, via setCurrentPageAsync. This is not a style preference — it is the only method that returns a complete tree. Walking several pages in a single invocation (whether by setCurrentPageAsync or by PageNode.loadAsync, and even after loading every page up front) returns PARTIAL and NON-DETERMINISTIC results: Navbar reported 2885 bound properties per-page, but 1685 and then 1669 on two batched runs of identical code. findAll(() => true) returned the same node count both ways, so the shortfall is invisible to a node-count sanity check. Any future re-sweep that batches pages will silently under-report and must not be used to refresh this file.",
  "$caveat": "Per-page TOTALS are not stable across library re-syncs. Between the first census and this one, Navbar went 3223 → 3510 properties (gaining 219 remote bindings) and Inputs went 1526 → 1155 (losing 339), with no edit of mine touching either count. Repeated reads within one session are byte-identical, so this is Figma re-resolving remote/library instance subtrees, not read noise. Consequence: a page's totals may move without anyone editing it, so the ratchet can report a false regression after a library re-sync. When that happens, confirm no real binding changed and re-baseline. A future improvement is to count only AUTHORABLE nodes (those outside any instance), which is both stable and free of double-counting — Navbar authorable-only was byte-identical across independent invocations.",
